 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nFeatures\n\nSimulation is performed according to the following rules that apply to all profile time slices that are assigned to a time-of-use rate\nin the simulation period:\n\nZero values in disconnection period\n\nsynthetic profile adjusted to\n\nbilled annual consumption\n\nsynthetic profile adjusted to\nperiod consumption of interval meter\n\nTime-of-Use Simulation Rules for Externally Saved Profile Values\n\nStep 1: Zero Values in Disconnection Period\n\nThe billing program checks whether the interval meter has been disconnected during the simulation period. The system observes\n\ndisconnections with the disconnection statuses 02 - Lowered/lLimited and03 - Disconnected. It is assumed that the\ndisconnection period has zero consumption, meaning that the profile values are set to zero.\n\nStep 2: Adjust Synthetic Profile to Measured Annual Consumption\n\nFor the remaining simulation period, the system uses a synthetic profile to generate the profile values. The synthetic profile is\ndetermined using the consumption pattern specified in the time-of-use interface. The synthetic profile has a standardized annual\n\nconsumption and therefore has to be adjusted to the annual consumption of the customer. The billing program attempts to\ndetermine the measured annual consumption for the profile by aggregating the existing measured total consumptions from MDUS\nrequests. The system uses MDUS requests from the representative period according to the percentage minimum share in the rate.\nChanges to the period consumption mean that consumptions from MDUS requests from older periods are not used.\n\n1 Note\n\nYou can use the method DETERMINE_CONTRACTS in the BADI ISU_FASTEDM_TOU_SIMULATION to influence the contract\nperiods from which MDUS requests can be observed.\n\nAggregation of the total consumption from MDUS requests does not have to take place for an entire year, but is based ona\npercentage minimum share in the rate. The synthetic profile is also used for the extrapolation of aggregated consumption values\nfor a year.\n\nStep 3: Synthetic Profile Adjusted to Period Consumption of Interval Meter\n\nIf it is not possible to determine the annual consumption measured (step 2 does not produce a result), the program uses the\n",
